# Feature & Module Templates

## index.ts — Feature

```ts
export * from "./components";
export * from "./hooks/use<FeatureName>";
export * from "./hooks/use<FeatureName>Mutations";
export type * from "./types";
```

## index.ts — Shared Module

```ts
export * from "./hooks/use<Domain>Table";
export * from "./hooks/queries/use<Domain>List";
export * from "./hooks/mutations/useAdd<Domain>";
export * from "./components";
export * from "./services";
export type * from "./types";
```

## components/index.ts — Feature or Module

```ts
export { CustomersTable } from "./customersTable.component";
export { CustomersTableFilters } from "./customersTableFilters.component";
```

Each component file: `components/<domain>.component.tsx` — export name stays `PascalCase`.

## types/index.ts — Feature or Module

```ts
export type { CustomersFilters } from "./customerFilters.types";
export type { GetCustomersParams } from "./getCustomersParams.types";
```

Each domain file: `types/<domain>.types.ts` — **never** `filterType.ts` or files without `.types.ts`.

## schemas/index.ts — Feature

```ts
import { z } from "zod";

export const <featureName>FormSchema = z.object({
  // fields matching API / form shape
});

export type <FeatureName>FormValues = z.infer<typeof <featureName>FormSchema>;
```

## schema.ts — Shared Module

```ts
import { z } from "zod";

export const <domain>FormSchema = z.object({
  // fields for add/edit modal
});

export type <Domain>FormValues = z.infer<typeof <domain>FormSchema>;
```

## types/ — single-domain file example

```
types/postsFilters.types.ts   ← filters shape
types/index.ts                ← re-exports
```

## Example — `posts` Feature

```
src/features/posts/
├── components/  PostList.tsx, PostForm.tsx
├── hooks/       usePosts.ts, usePostMutations.ts
├── schemas/     index.ts
├── types/       index.ts
├── pages/       PostsPage.tsx
└── index.ts
```

Consumers: `import { PostList, useCreatePost } from "@/features/posts";`

Router (pages imported directly, not via index):

```ts
const PostsPage = React.lazy(() =>
  import("@/features/posts/pages/PostsPage").then((m) => ({
    default: m.PostsPage,
  })),
);
```

## Example — `CustomersModule` (canonical shared module)

Reference implementation after refactor — follow this layout for new table modules:

```
src/shared/modules/CustomersModule/
├── components/
│   ├── customersTable.component.tsx
│   ├── customersTableFilters.component.tsx
│   ├── customersModelFilter.component.tsx
│   ├── customersFilterToolbar.component.tsx
│   └── index.ts
├── columns/
│   └── customerColumns.tsx          ← useCustomerTableColumns, inline column defs
├── constants/
│   ├── initialFilters.ts
│   └── filters.ts                   ← useCustomerFilterItems
├── hooks/
│   ├── useCustomersTable.ts         ← orchestration + infinity fetchFn
│   ├── queries/
│   │   ├── useCustomersMetrics.ts
│   │   ├── useCustomerAnalytics.ts
│   │   └── useCustomerOrders.ts
│   └── mutations/                   ← when module has mutations
├── services/
│   ├── getCustomers.service.ts
│   ├── getCustomerOrders.service.ts
│   ├── getCustomerOrdersByRole.service.ts
│   ├── getCustomerAnalyticsByRole.service.ts
│   ├── fetchCustomersPage.service.ts
│   └── index.ts
├── types/
│   ├── customerFilters.types.ts
│   ├── getCustomersParams.types.ts
│   └── index.ts
├── utils/
│   ├── buildCustomersQueryParams.ts
│   └── customerExport.ts
└── index.ts
```

Feature shell (`src/features/customers/`):

```
├── pages/CustomersPage.tsx   ← thin: renders <CustomersTable /> from module
└── index.ts                  ← empty or hooks only — no page export
```

Shared hook used across modules: `src/shared/hooks/useCitySearch.ts`

Tests: `tests/shared/modules/CustomersModule/**` (mirror `src/` — never co-located in `src/`)

## Example — `BranchesModule` (table module with mutations)

```
src/shared/modules/BranchesModule/
├── hooks/
│   ├── useBranchesTable.ts          ← orchestration + infinity fetchFn
│   ├── useBranchModals.ts
│   ├── useBranchUpsertForm.ts
│   ├── queries/
│   │   ├── useBranchList.ts
│   │   └── useBranchPharmacistsInfinite.ts
│   └── mutations/
│       ├── useAddBranch.ts
│       ├── useUpdateBranch.ts
│       ├── useBranchDeletion.ts
│       └── useBranchLinkWithMeta.ts
└── index.ts                         ← re-export queries + mutations via barrel
```

## Example — `InventoryModule` (legacy — migrate toward CustomersModule pattern)

```
src/shared/modules/InventoryModule/
├── components/   inventoryTable.component.tsx, …
├── hooks/        useInventoryTable.ts, useInventoryFilters.ts
│   ├── queries/    useInventoryList.ts (when migrated)
│   └── mutations/  useUpdateProductStatus.ts
├── services/     getInventoryProducts.service.ts, index.ts
├── columns/      columns.tsx
├── constants/    initialFilters.ts, filters.ts
├── types/        *.types.ts, index.ts
├── utils/        filterValidationUtils.ts
└── index.ts
```

Consumers: `import { InventoryTable, useInventoryTable } from "@/shared/modules/InventoryModule";`

Feature page composes the module:

```tsx
import { InventoryTable } from "@/shared/modules/InventoryModule";
```

## DO

- Create `index.ts` first — define the public API before implementation
- **Features:** keep routes/pages thin; compose from `@/shared/modules/*` when domain UI is reused
- **Modules:** co-locate `services/`, `columns/`, `constants/`, `modals/` inside the module
- **No response mappers** in `utils/` when `@/shared/types/dtos/` matches the API — use backend fields in columns/UI
- Table logic in `use<Domain>Table` — state, `querySignature`, and `useCallback` fetch fn → `fetch<Domain>Page.service`
- Keep Zod in `schemas/index.ts` (features) or `schema.ts` (modules)
- Lazy-load feature page components from the router

## DON'T

- Import deep paths — use `@/features/<name>` or `@/shared/modules/<Module>`
- Put domain tables/modals in a feature when used in 2+ places — extract to a module
- Put generic UI in features or modules — move to `src/components/ui/`
- Nest `components/` inside `components/` (max one level of child components — see `02-patterns/002-ui-components.mdc`)
- Export page components from feature `index.ts`
- Import `src/features/*` from inside a shared module
- Add `*.mapper.ts` or `*Mapper.ts` in module `utils/` when the backend already returns the correct DTO shape
- Put `useCitySearch`-style hooks inside a single module when 2+ modules need them — use `src/shared/hooks/`
- Create empty `types/`, `schemas/`, or `pages/` folders
